Use ApplicationServices rather than CoreGraphics directly.

Before macOS 10.8 there is no top-level CoreGraphics.framework: CoreGraphics
is a sub-framework of ApplicationServices.framework. That affects both halves
of the reference -- -framework CoreGraphics does not link, and
<CoreGraphics/CoreGraphics.h> does not resolve either, since the headers live
under ApplicationServices.framework/Frameworks/ as well.

The ApplicationServices umbrella re-exports CoreGraphics and includes its
headers, and is present on every macOS release, so this is safe everywhere.
CoreFoundation and IOKit, also used by this port, are top-level frameworks on
all releases and need no equivalent change.

--- system/resolution.v.original
+++ system/resolution.v
@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@
 module system
 
-#flag darwin -framework IOKit -framework CoreGraphics
+#flag darwin -framework IOKit -framework ApplicationServices
 
-#include <CoreGraphics/CoreGraphics.h>
+#include <ApplicationServices/ApplicationServices.h>
 #include <IOKit/graphics/IOGraphicsLib.h>
 
 // Define necessary types and constants
